      "body": "**Security issue**  \n\ud83d\uded1 Blocker \u2014 must fix before merge\n\n**Known vulnerabilities in vite@5.4.0**\n\nOSV.dev reports 15 known vulnerabilities affecting `vite@5.4.0`, introduced by this PR:\n\n- [GHSA-356w-63v5-8wf4](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-32395) **moderate**: Vite has an `server.fs.deny` bypass with an invalid `request-target` \u2014 fixed in 6.2.6, 6.1.5, 6.0.15, 5.4.18, 4.5.13\n- [GHSA-4r4m-qw57-chr8](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-31125) **moderate**: Vite has a `server.fs.deny` bypassed for `inline` and `raw` with `?import` query \u2014 fixed in 6.2.4, 6.1.3, 6.0.13, 5.4.16, 4.5.11\n- [GHSA-4w7w-66w2-5vf9](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-39365) **moderate**: Vite Vulnerable to Path Traversal in Optimized Deps `.map` Handling \u2014 fixed in 8.0.5, 7.3.2, 6.4.2\n\n\u2026and 12 more \u2014 see the OSV links above.\n\nUpgrade to 6.2.6, 6.1.5, 6.0.15, 5.4.18, 4.5.13 or later.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn devfn/docs/package.json, upgrade the dependency vite from 5.4.0 to a non-vulnerable version (0.1.24, 2.14.1, 2.9.0, 3.2.11, 4.5.10, 4.5.11, 4.5.12, 4.5.13, 4.5.14, 4.5.4, 4.5.6, 5.2.14, 5.3.6, 5.4.12, 5.4.15, 5.4.16, 5.4.17, 5.4.18, 5.4.19, 5.4.20, 5.4.21, 5.4.6, 5.4.9, 6.0.12, 6.0.13, 6.0.14, 6.0.15, 6.0.9, 6.1.2, 6.1.3, 6.1.4, 6.1.5, 6.1.6, 6.2.3, 6.2.4, 6.2.5, 6.2.6, 6.2.7, 6.3.4, 6.3.6, 6.4.1, 6.4.2, 6.4.3, 7.0.7, 7.0.8, 7.1.11, 7.1.5, 7.3.2, 7.3.5, 8.0.16, 8.0.5). Update any associated lockfile entries.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n> Not useful? Reply `@mira-rhombus reject` to dismiss this suggestion.",
